<title>USA: Cablevision to sell $1 bln in systems - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Cablevision to sell $1 bln in systems - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cablevision Systems Corp is planning to put nearly $1 billion in cable systems up for sale, the Wall Street Journal reported in its Thursday electronic edition.</p>
<p>The company told analysts in a conference call that it would &quot;monetize non-strategic assets,&quot; primarily cable systems serving 475,000 cable customers in non-core markets, the report said.</p>
<p>Cablevision Chief Executive James Dolan did not indicate any sale was imminent but said proceeds would be used to reduce the company's $4 billion debt, the report said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
